\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  Go on Strike at DHL Cargo Hub\b0\par\par\uc2 By Liz Young \par \uc2 439 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 December 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 More than 1,100 union workers at \uc2 DHL\uc2 's air cargo hub at the Cincinnati/Northern Kentucky International Airport walked off the job Thursday, a move that affects one of the parcel carrier's largest logistics facilities during the busiest shipping season of the year.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Brotherhood of Teamsters\uc2  said its members are protesting unfair labor practices at the hub run by \uc2 DHL Express\uc2 , a U.S. unit of German logistics giant \uc2 Deutsche Post\uc2  that handles express parcel business.\par \par \uc2 DHL Express\uc2  said the company anticipated the job action and has enacted contingency plans such as bringing on replacement staff and moving flights and volume to other \uc2 DHL\uc2  locations across the U.S.\par \par \uc2 The company said it is expecting job actions at some of its other pickup and delivery locations across the U.S. in support of the Cincinnati hub strike and plans to bring on replacement staff in those areas.\par \par \uc2 "As a result of these contingencies, we do not anticipate any significant disruptions to our service performance," a \uc2 DHL\uc2  representative said.\par \par \uc2 The Cincinnati hub is one of \uc2 DHL\uc2 's three so-called global superhubs, with the others in Hong Kong and Leipzig, Germany. The Midwestern hub handles an average of 350,000 packages a day with 130 daily flights and a fleet of 60 aircraft.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  have been negotiating with \uc2 DHL\uc2  to establish a union contract at the Cincinnati airport since July after the workers who load and unload planes at the facility, known as ramp and tug workers, voted to unionize in April. The union represents more than 6,000 \uc2 DHL\uc2  workers across the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Union leaders have filed complaints of unfair labor practices against \uc2 DHL\uc2 , alleging workers at the Cincinnati hub were punished or fired for engaging in union activities. A local \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  general counsel later added allegations that \uc2 DHL\uc2  surveilled workers discussing the union off-site and interfered with efforts to unionize.\par \par \uc2 DHL\uc2  declined to comment on the allegations. It has previously said the company recognizes employees' right to unionize within the confines of the law and that it is committed to the agreements it has with its local, national and international labor partners.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 DHL\uc2  job action comes as workers across the U.S., from package-delivery drivers to warehouse staff, have called for better pay and recognition for showing up through the Covid-19 pandemic when other employees could work remotely. A series of labor agreements reached this year has delivered big wage increases, including for auto workers, airline pilots and dockworkers at West Coast ports.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020231208ejc80003i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
