\par\par \b \uc2 EXCHANGE --- \uc2 Amazon\uc2  Faces Black Friday Strikes, Protests\b0\par\par\uc2 By Helena Smolak \par \uc2 601 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 November 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B9\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Amazon.com\uc2  faced strikes in the U.S. and Europe on Black Friday, hitting the e-commerce giant at the start of the busy holiday shopping weekend as labor unrest picks up on both sides of the Atlantic.\par \par \uc2 Warehouse workers and drivers planned strikes Friday in the U.S., the U.K., Germany, Italy and Spain to demand better wages and working conditions, according to the \uc2 UNI Global Union\uc2 , a global union federation focused on the services sector with affiliated organizations from 150 countries. Further protests by climate activists and workers are planned in other countries, the \uc2 UNI Global Union\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The planned demonstrations could disrupt supply chains and prevent merchandise from reaching \uc2 Amazon\uc2  on Black Friday as the U.S. e-commerce giant aims to boost sales. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  had advertised 10 days of holiday discounts from Nov. 17 to Nov. 27.\par \par \uc2 An Amazon Germany spokesman said strikes wouldn't affect deliveries.\par \par \uc2 "We offer great pay and benefits for our employees, with great career opportunities, and provide a modern and safe working environment for all," an Amazon U.K. spokesman said.\par \par \uc2 The industrial action is part of a global campaign known as "Make \uc2 Amazon\uc2  Pay" coordinated by the \uc2 UNI Global Union\uc2 , which expects strikes, protests and other action in more than 30 countries.\par \par \uc2 This is the fourth year that the campaign has taken place, but this time the protests come against a background of rising labor unrest in developed economies. The U.S. has seen walkouts in industries ranging from auto making to entertainment, while labor protests swept several European economies earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 In Germany, \uc2 Amazon\uc2 's second-biggest market by sales in 2022, employees at five fulfillment centers in Bad Hersfeld, Dortmund, Koblenz, Leipzig, and Rheinberg, began a 24-hour strike at midnight on Thursday to demand a collective wage agreement, \uc2 trade union Ver.di\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 "Employees will continue to fight with great commitment for a collective wage and health agreement. The exploitation of \uc2 Amazon\uc2  employees must come to an end," \uc2 Ver.di\uc2  spokesman Jan Jurczyk said.\par \par \uc2 An \uc2 Amazon\uc2  spokesman said employees in Germany are paid fair wages, with a starting gross salary of more than 14 euros ($15.27) an hour, including additional benefits.\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2 's employees in Germany report pressure to perform and intense workloads and surveillance that creates a climate of fear, Silke Zimmer, a member of the \uc2 Ver.di\uc2  national executive board, said.\par \par \uc2 "We reject the trade union's criticism as it does not reflect reality. It's not for nothing that half of our colleagues have been with us for over five years," an Amazon Germany spokesman told The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 More than 1,000 workers at an \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouse in Coventry, England went on strike Friday, the \uc2 GMB Union\uc2  said. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  was hit by its first strike in the U.K. earlier this year in a dispute over pay.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Italian and Spanish trade unions CGIL and CCOO used social media to call for strikes over the Black Friday weekend. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers in India also demonstrated, the \uc2 UNI Global Union\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UNI Global Union\uc2  said protests are expected in Japan, Netherlands, Germany, Ireland, Italy, the U.K. and Canada against the climate impact of \uc2 Amazon\uc2 's data centers, it said. In France, anticapitalist group Attac called for protests targeting \uc2 Amazon\uc2 's parcel lockers on social media.\par \par \uc2 An \uc2 Amazon\uc2  spokesperson said the company has invested billions of dollars in packaging reduction and purchases of renewable energy and electric vehicles as part of its target to achieve net zero carbon emissions by 2040.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020231125ejbp00011\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
