\par\par \b \uc2 Tesla\uc2  Raises Wages in Germany as Union Presses\b0\par\par\uc2 By William Boston \par \uc2 976 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 November 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BERLIN -- \uc2 Tesla\uc2  is boosting factory worker pay in Germany amid an aggressive unionization drive, a move that comes as Chief Executive \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  may face similar organizing attempts in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Tesla\uc2 's management in Germany late last week unveiled a package of wage increases for workers during Musk's visit to the "Gigafactory" on the outskirts of Berlin, \uc2 Tesla\uc2  said on Monday. Musk also promised the assembly plant would build its next-generation vehicle. The company said the pay increases are part of a routine review of wages at the factory. "Claims that there is a connection between \uc2 Tesla\uc2 's salary adjustments and union activities are untrue," \uc2 Tesla\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Tesla\uc2  has been under pressure from Germany's powerful \uc2 IG Metall union\uc2 , which is trying to organize the plant and get \uc2 Tesla\uc2  to agree to a union contract. In Sweden, a smaller industrial union representing \uc2 Tesla\uc2  service workers has been on strike as it pursues a collective-bargaining contract.\par \par \uc2 The announcements come as the \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2  eyes \uc2 Tesla\uc2 's factories in the U.S. After winning record contracts from Detroit automakers, the union is betting it will attract nonunionized workers to its ranks. Shortly after the \uc2 UAW\uc2 's wins, \uc2 Toyota\uc2  said last week it was raising wages for most of its U.S. auto-factory workers, who aren't unionized.\par \par \uc2 The unionization of \uc2 Tesla\uc2  workers in the U.S. and Europe would threaten to further increase the company's labor costs when its profit is already under pressure and as it slashes prices in response to slowing growth. Workers in general have been agitating for richer paychecks amid heightened costs of living and a new wave of labor activism.\par \par \uc2 Tesla\uc2  said Monday that executives had informed workers during a "team huddle" with Musk on Friday that the company would raise wages by 4% effective in November for the around 11,000 employees at the German plant. \uc2 Tesla\uc2  will also pay a bonus equivalent to about $1,600 in December to offset inflation. That comes on top of an inflation-adjustment bonus of the same size last year, exhausting the legal limit in Germany for tax-free adjustments. Starting in February, \uc2 Tesla\uc2  will raise annual wages by an additional amount equivalent to about $2,680 for workers in production.\par \par \uc2 "At Giga Berlin today to congratulate the team on their excellent progress. The factory looks amazing! We are going to cover all the concrete with art," Musk wrote on X, formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , Friday.\par \par \uc2 During his visit, Musk also promised that \uc2 Tesla\uc2 's new next-generation electric car would be produced at the German factory after a planned expansion next year, according to people with knowledge of his comments.\par \par \uc2 The new wage increases follow a 6% wage increase after the opening of the plant last year, according to \uc2 IG Metall\uc2 . The plant produces about 5,000 cars a week, according to company statements issued earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 The wage increases follow heightened tension between \uc2 Tesla\uc2  and \uc2 IG Metall\uc2 , Germany's largest labor union, and a separate confrontation with \uc2 Tesla\uc2  service-center workers in Sweden.\par \par \uc2 Tesla\uc2  is the only major carmaker in Europe without union representation on the shop floor. Musk has criticized unions on X and has said that \uc2 Tesla\uc2  pays higher factory-worker compensation than rivals.\par \par \uc2 Last month, \uc2 IG Metall\uc2  said 1,000 employees at the plant donned union badges on the job and protested working conditions. The union wouldn't say how many \uc2 Tesla\uc2  workers are now members, but it has stepped up outreach efforts in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 "We want union contract terms at \uc2 Tesla\uc2  and so do the \uc2 Tesla\uc2  employees," said \uc2 Christiane Benner\uc2 , chairwoman of \uc2 IG Metall\uc2 , last month.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 IG Metall\uc2 , \uc2 Tesla\uc2  management first told workers at the plant about coming wage increases in October, after the union staged a week of protests and round-the-clock outreach to \uc2 Tesla\uc2  workers during shift changes.\par \par \uc2 When \uc2 IG Metall\uc2  had arranged a visit on Oct. 9 to talk to workers inside the plant during their lunch break, a right that the union says is guaranteed under German labor law, \uc2 Tesla\uc2  management invited workers to a free lunch and promised a surprise for the same time, \uc2 IG Metall\uc2  said in an Oct. 11 statement.\par \par \uc2 During the lunch, \uc2 Tesla\uc2  management passed out free T-shirts and told employees that there would be a detailed announcement in November outlining wage increases, according to \uc2 IG Metall\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Dirk Schulze, the regional \uc2 IG Metall\uc2  director leading efforts to organize \uc2 Tesla\uc2 , called the wage increase and bonuses an important step in a longer effort to boost pay, but added that improvements in working conditions and wages need to be guaranteed in a union contract, as is common at other manufacturers.\par \par \uc2 Schulze said \uc2 Tesla\uc2  monthly wages are lower than what is typically paid at other German automakers. He said \uc2 Tesla\uc2  also doesn't pay bonuses for summer vacation or Christmas, which are a routine part of union contracts at other automakers in Germany.\par \par \uc2 "If you compare annual wages there is a big gap between \uc2 Tesla\uc2  and our union workers at \uc2 Porsche\uc2 , \uc2 BMW\uc2 , \uc2 Audi\uc2 , VW, \uc2 Daimler\uc2  and Ford," he said.\par \par \uc2 An \uc2 IG Metall\uc2  spokesman said the union was focused on the election next year of a new works council at \uc2 Tesla\uc2 , an internal committee of labor representatives who have broad say in company policies including working conditions and hiring and firing of employees. The works council isn't allowed to negotiate wages.\par \par \uc2 IG Metall\uc2  said that the current works council at \uc2 Tesla\uc2 's German factory, elected early last year, is made up largely of lower-level leadership employees who are close to executive management. The union aims to get members elected to the council in the next election, expected to take place next year.\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 Tim Higgins contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020231107ejb70001q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
