\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. News: Teachers Strike in Portland, Ore., Closes Schools for 45,000 Pupils\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 290 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 November 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Teachers in Portland, Ore., went on strike Wednesday, prompting the district to close school for more than 45,000 students.\par \par \uc2 The Portland Association of Teachers said it was the first time the union, representing more than 4,000 educators, had gone on strike. The union and Portland Public Schools have failed to agree on compensation, classroom size limits and other issues in their latest contract negotiations.\par \par \uc2 District officials have said the union's requests aren't financially feasible, in part because state funding hasn't kept up with inflation. There is a more than $200 million difference between the union's proposal and their own, the district said.\par \par \uc2 Union workers have flexed their power this year with work stoppages across industries, including Hollywood, the auto industry and healthcare. Strikes have also shut down public schools in other cities.\par \par \uc2 It is unclear how long the Portland strike, which affects 81 schools, will last.\par \par \uc2 The district said it is offering educators a 10.9% cost-of-living increase over three years, while the union has asked for a cumulative 23% cost-of-living increase. District officials said in a press briefing Wednesday they have been working within the constraints of their budget during months of negotiations with the union. The union's proposal, superintendent Guadalupe Guerrero said, could result in staffing cuts, which could lead to higher class sizes and reduced services for students. District leaders urged state lawmakers to provide more funding.\par \par \uc2 "Funding has not kept pace with the needs of our students, nor our educators," Guerrero said.\par \par \uc2 "Unlike a private organization," he added, "we don't have record profits we can tap into."\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020231102ejb20001d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
