\par\par \b \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  Lost $3.2 Billion Due to Workers' Walkout --- Auto giant reports rise in quarterly sales, vehicle shipments\b0\par\par\uc2 By David Sachs \par \uc2 396 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 November 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Chrysler parent \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  said the strike by U.S. auto workers had cost it more than $3 billion in lost revenue as it reported a rise in quarterly sales.\par \par \uc2 The update from \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 , which also makes the \uc2 Jeep\uc2  and Dodge brands, is the latest indication of the financial fallout from a six-week strike that put 45,000 workers on the picket lines.\par \par \uc2 The strike ended Monday after \uc2 General Motors\uc2  reached a tentative labor deal with the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2 , following similar pacts with \uc2 Ford Motor\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  said Tuesday that production losses from the dispute equated to around 3 billion euros, equivalent to $3.2 billion, in lost revenue. The effect of the strike on the company's profit was under 750 million euros, Chief Financial Officer Natalie Knight said on a call with reporters.\par \par \uc2 The profit hit related to the strike was lower than those absorbed by Ford and GM, which reported $1.3 billion and $800 million profit losses, respectively.\par \par \uc2 "For us, we are a big global company, so [North America] is part of the scheme but it's very different than what it is for our competitors," Knight said.\par \par \uc2 Details on the financial toll of the \uc2 UAW\uc2  strike came as \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  reported a rise in third-quarter revenue to 45.10 billion euros from 42.10 billion euros in the same period last year.\par \par \uc2 The Netherlands-based company said the revenue figure, which beat analysts' expectations, reflected improved volume and steady pricing, though the gains were partially offset by currency exchange rates.\par \par \uc2 Consolidated vehicle shipments rose 11% to 1.4 million, driven by growth in Europe, the Middle East and Africa, North America and South America, \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Total new vehicle inventory stood at 1.4 million vehicles on Sept. 30. The company's inventory of 388,000 vehicles was 158,000 higher than it was at the end of 2022 because of what the company called a normalization after years of supply-chain constraints.\par \par \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  confirmed its full-year guidance of an adjusted operating income margin in the double digits and positive free cash flow.\par \par \uc2 Knight also said investors can expect to hear more about cost-savings measures beyond pulling out of various trade shows, measures that were previously announced.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020231101ejb10001m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
