\par\par \uc2 Heard on the Street\par \b \uc2 Auto Strikes Leave a Sweetheart Deal on Car Dealers\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jinjoo Lee \par \uc2 538 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 October 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B10\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 [Financial Analysis and Commentary]\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  strikes in Detroit have been costly for automakers. Car dealers barely got a scratch, but their stock prices don't reflect that.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, \uc2 Ford Motor\uc2  reached a tentative deal with the union, and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  did so as well on Saturday. Although the \uc2 UAW\uc2  has expanded its strike at \uc2 General Motors\uc2 , a drawn-out strike now appears less likely.\par \par \uc2 This is a best-case scenario for dealers, for whom the threat of prolonged strikes actually might have led to better margins on some car sales.\par \par \uc2 Asbury Automotive\uc2 , a small dealer group, said dealers scaled back on discounts for domestic-brand vehicles after the strikes began.\par \par \uc2 A longer strike would have ruined dealers' high-margin parts-and-service business. Service, body and parts account for 10% to 15% of dealers' revenue but 30% to 35% of gross profit.\par \par \uc2 The service, body and parts segment is a needs-based business -- seen as a hedge from economic cycles. At \uc2 Lithia Motors\uc2 , for example, it is the only segment that has seen year-over-year same-store revenue growth for the past 10 consecutive quarters. \uc2 AutoNation\uc2  on Friday reported that it is seeing "significant benefits" from its focus on after-sales services, which saw record revenues and margins in the third quarter.\par \par \uc2 A report from \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  had noted that strikes could hit dealers' parts and service sales and new-vehicle volumes if they lasted through the end of November. Additionally, a shift in sales to foreign brands -- such as \uc2 Toyota\uc2 , \uc2 Nissan\uc2  or \uc2 Honda\uc2  -- would weigh on margins because their vehicles carry lower gross profit per unit, the report noted.\par \par \uc2 The larger dealer groups aren't fretting about any parts or vehicle shortages just yet. Both \uc2 AutoNation\uc2  and \uc2 Lithia\uc2  said there wasn't much of an immediate impact and said they pre-emptively stockpiled parts. Asbury did note that it wasn't receiving shipments from manufacturers in some cases.\par \par \uc2 A resolution to the \uc2 UAW\uc2  negotiations now appears in sight, but dealers' share prices aren't fully reflecting the progress made. Even with the share-price rebound following the news of Ford's tentative deal with the union, the three dealers -- Asbury, \uc2 AutoNation\uc2  and \uc2 Lithia\uc2  -- with the highest exposure to the Detroit Three automakers have logged the biggest stock-price slides since \uc2 UAW\uc2  strikes hit parts distribution centers on Sept. 22. The three have dropped 16% on average since Sept. 22.\par \par \uc2 Dealers have a lot of other speed bumps to deal with. Rising interest rates are hurting vehicle affordability for prospective car buyers, with the average interest rate on loans for new cars rising to 7.4% in the third quarter -- the highest since 2007, according to Edmunds.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 Cox Automotive\uc2 , new-car inventory was up 60% as of early October compared with the same time a year ago, taking it back to the highest level since the spring of 2021. High rates and recovering inventories are adding up to some hefty payments dealers must make to finance their inventory.\par \par \uc2 Still, barring an unexpected snag in \uc2 UAW\uc2  negotiations, dealers now have one more obstacle they don't have to worry about.\par \par \uc2 page,5043 \par \par \uc2 Document J000000020231030ejau0000o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
