\par\par \b \uc2 EXCHANGE --- \uc2 GM\uc2 , \uc2 UAW\uc2  Move Closer to Tentative Labor Agreement\b0\par\par\uc2 By Mike Colias \par \uc2 465 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 October 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2  is close to completing a tentative agreement on a new contract with \uc2 General Motors\uc2 , two days after the union clinched a tentative deal with \uc2 Ford Motor\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The two sides negotiated throughout Thursday night and into Friday morning, and reconvened in the early afternoon in a push to secure a deal, people with knowledge of the talks said. \uc2 GM\uc2  presented an offer overnight that is similar to the tentative agreement that the union struck with Ford on Wednesday, the people said.\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2  President Shawn Fain and \uc2 GM\uc2  Chief Executive \uc2 Mary Barra\uc2  met along with negotiators for several hours on Thursday, the people said, cautioning that it is unclear if a deal is imminent because the talks are fluid. Union negotiators also are bargaining Friday with Chrysler-parent \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 , according to people familiar with those talks. Around 28,000 workers from the two companies remain on strike as the companies work to secure separate tentative agreements.\par \par \uc2 The union on Wednesday struck a tentative agreement with Ford that included a 25% wage increase spread out over four years, including 11% in the first year. Union leaders told the roughly 16,600 Ford members who had been on strike to return to work pending the vote on the tentative contract, which is expected in the next week or two. The decision to have members leave the picket lines was in part meant to pressure \uc2 GM\uc2  and Chrysler-maker \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  to move closer to the \uc2 UAW\uc2 's demands.\par \par \uc2 The union's tentative agreement with Ford, which covers 57,000 \uc2 UAW\uc2 -represented workers, also included a return of cost-of-living adjustments that the union gave up in 2009, as well as enhanced retirement benefits. The \uc2 UAW\uc2 's head of bargaining for \uc2 GM\uc2 , Mike Booth, told leaders from the union's local chapters during a conference call Thursday that several items remain under discussion, including retirement benefits and wages, people with knowledge of the meeting said.\par \par \uc2 Workers remain on strike at \uc2 GM\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  across five assembly plants and dozens of parts-distribution centers.\par \par \uc2 Shares of all three companies sold off on Friday. Ford's stock fell 12% following its third-quarter earnings report Thursday evening that fell short of analysts' expectations.\par \par \uc2 GM\uc2  shares fell nearly 5%. The company's driverless-car operator, Cruise, said it would suspend all service after a California regulator pulled its permit to run driverless taxis. \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  shares declined about 2%\par \par \uc2 The financial toll of the shutdowns is mounting for the companies. \uc2 GM\uc2  has said the strike is costing it $200 million a week in lost profit. That figure was before the union called a walkout Tuesday of \uc2 GM\uc2 's 5,000-employee truck factory in Arlington, Texas, its largest plant.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020231028ejas0002h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
